# Nothing here is a substitute for the gitleaks pre-commit hook: .gitignore
# cannot help with a secret pasted into a file that IS tracked. It exists to keep
# the machine-local half of the split out, and to make the adjacency risk explicit.

# ── The machine-local half ───────────────────────────────────
# Created by hand during install and never committed. The .example files are.
machine.zsh
statusline.sh

# ── Credential files, by name ────────────────────────────────
# None of these live under dotfiles/, so none can be reached by the symlink loop
# in INSTALL.md. Listed anyway: the cost is one line each, and the failure they
# guard against is permanent.
secrets.zsh
.netrc
.pypirc
hosts.yml
credentials
rclone.conf
*token*
*.pem
*.key
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*

# ── Claude Code runtime state ────────────────────────────────
# settings.local.json and .claude.json sit beside tracked files, which is the
# only genuine adjacency risk in the layout. shell-snapshots is the sharp one:
# it freezes the shell environment at session start, tokens included.
# The **/ prefix is load-bearing: a pattern containing a slash is anchored to
# this file's directory, so a bare `.claude/…` would never match the real path
# `dotfiles/claude/.claude/…`.
**/.claude/settings.local.json
**/.claude.json
**/.claude.json.backup
**/.claude/shell-snapshots/
**/.claude/projects/
**/.claude/plugins/
**/.claude/security/
**/.claude/file-history/
**/.claude/transcripts/
**/.claude/memory/
**/.claude/cache/
**/.claude/backups/
**/.claude/teams/
**/.claude/telemetry/
**/.claude/jobs/
**/.claude/statsig/
**/.claude/todos/
**/.claude/append.md

# ── Install residue ──────────────────────────────────────────
*.bak
*.bak.*
*.orig
*~

# ── OS and editor ────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/

# Completion caches — hostname-specific, regenerated on every shell start.
.zcompdump*

# review reports and team config — working notes, not part of the environment
.flw/
